    longDescription:
      "The IncStores Dashboard is a production-ready, enterprise-style analytics application for eCommerce teams who need a single pane of glass for revenue, sales, products, customers, customizations, and web analytics. It connects directly to a MySQL database (e.g. Magento/IncStores schema), offers AI-powered natural language queries via an in-app chatbot, integrates Google Analytics–style metrics, and delivers board-ready KPIs through an Executive Center and multiple intelligence modules. The stack is React 18 + TypeScript + Vite on the frontend and Node.js + Express on the backend, with a dark theme, smooth animations (Framer Motion), and responsive layout.\n\nTechnology stack and architecture\n\n• Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Vite 5, Tailwind CSS 3, Recharts 3, Framer Motion 12, Lucide React, Axios, date-fns 4.\n• Backend: Node.js, Express 4, TypeScript (tsx); REST API on port 3001; health check at /health with DB status.\n• Database: MySQL (mysql2) for orders, products, customers, quotes, product views, and report tables.\n• AI / NLP: Groq SDK (LLM) for natural language to SQL in the chatbot; only SELECT queries, safe execution.\n• Optional: Supabase, Vercel serverless for auth/deployment. CORS configurable via CORS_ORIGINS.\n\nCore dashboard modules\n\n• Overview (Dashboard Home): Executive summary with KPI cards (revenue, orders), revenue and order trends (line charts), top products with drill-down, category performance (pie/bar), recent activity, customer segments, new vs repeat revenue, financial KPIs. Date range, country, payment method, store, and customer group filters; CSV export for top products, categories, and activity.\n• Sales: Deep dive into revenue, velocity, and forecasting—overview (revenue, order count, AOV), trends, top products, category mix, hourly sales; same filter set as overview.\n• Products: Catalog performance, product views, search analytics (popular searches, no-results), top unpurchased products, category distribution; drill-down to Product Detail (single product metrics, trends, orders).\n• Customers: Segments (e.g. VIP, regular, at-risk), retention, growth trends, top customers by revenue/orders; drill-down to Customer Detail (profile, order history, LTV).\n• Customizations: Bespoke order funnel, popular customization options, trends, breakdown by category; filters aligned with the rest of the app.\n\nIntelligence and strategic modules\n\n• Executive Center: Board-ready KPIs—health score gauge, critical alerts (e.g. revenue drop, catalog issues), quick wins, retention metrics, catalog health (active vs recent SKUs), recommendations, pipeline forecast (revenue and order forecast with historical comparison).\n• Revenue Intelligence: Forward-looking revenue signals—pipeline and forecast, new vs repeat revenue split, monthly revenue and trends, revenue by segment, order value distribution, recommendations.\n• Financial KPIs: Revenue growth rates, trend charts, key financial ratios.\n• Customer LTV: Lifetime value by segment/cohort, at-risk customers, time to second purchase, retention metrics.\n• Revenue per Visitor: RPV, conversion and traffic quality signals.\n• Demand Intelligence: Regional and seasonal demand forecasting, product velocity by region, 90-day demand forecast, inventory alerts, product trends, category surge forecast.\n• Product Catalog Health: Active vs dead/recent SKUs, dead products (no movement), product lifecycle, catalog quality alerts.\n• Google Analytics: GA4-style integration—traffic sources, trends, comparison, funnel, campaign and demographics, geo, device, landing page, session duration, bounce rate, conversion rate, user retention, eCommerce behavior; 40+ read endpoints plus optional sync.\n• B2B Intelligence: B2B-specific analytics, top B2B customers, revenue and order patterns for B2B segment.\n\nCross-cutting features\n\n• AI-powered chatbot: Users type questions in plain English; Groq generates a single SELECT query against the dashboard MySQL schema, runs it safely (no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE), and returns formatted results (summary, table, or JSON). Floating chat widget, conversation history, loading and error states.\n• Global search: Cmd+K / Ctrl+K overlay to jump to pages, apply filter presets (e.g. Last 30 days, High churn risk), and optionally search metrics/products.\n• Navigation and layout: Collapsible sidebar (icon-only vs full labels), Dashboard and Intelligence sections, active state with Framer Motion; header with menu and search; context-based view switching; AnimatePresence page transitions.\n• Data refresh and loading: Auto-refresh on key pages (e.g. Executive Center every 5 minutes); loading screens and skeletons; API error handling.\n• Filters and export: Centralized filter state (date range, country, payment, store, customer group) across sales, dashboard, products, customers, customizations; CSV export for tables with quantity modal.\n\nBackend API and design\n\nREST routes under /api: sales (overview, trends, top-products, categories, hourly, filters), products (performance, metrics, views, search-analytics, top-unpurchased, :id), customers (overview, segments, growth, top, by-segment, :id), customizations (metrics, popular, trends, by-category), dashboard (activity, metrics, filters, stats), intelligence (30+ endpoints for executive, pipeline, LTV, demand, catalog, B2B, financial, revenue-per-visitor), chatbot (POST /query for NL to SQL), google-analytics (40+ read endpoints + optional sync). Dark theme (background #1A1D24, accent #F76C2F); Recharts for line, bar, pie, area; responsive with mobile sidebar slide-over.\n\nDeployment\n\nFrontend: Vite build; deploy to Vercel or static host; set VITE_API_URL to backend base URL. Backend: Run on Railway, Render, or any Node host; set PORT, CORS_ORIGINS, GROQ_API_KEY, MySQL env vars. Database: MySQL with schema for sales_order, catalog_product_entity, customer_entity, quote, report_viewed_product_index, etc.",
