    tags: ["Admin", "Firebase", "React", "TypeScript", "Groq", "OneSignal", "Recharts", "Analytics", "Dashboard", "Mental Wellness"],
    longDescription:
      "Mindspace.ai is an admin dashboard for managing a mental health and wellness platform. It sits alongside Tara Calling (the user-facing PWA where people talk to the TARA AI companion) and Firebase Cloud Functions (backend services). Together they form a single ecosystem: users interact in the app, data lives in Firebase, and admins use the Mindspace.ai Dashboard to view analytics, manage users, send push notifications (including AI-generated ones), and monitor calls, assessments, and engagement.\n\nTech stack at a glance\n\n• Frontend: React 18.3.x (UI), TypeScript 5.5.x (type safety), Vite 5.4.x (build, dev server, fast HMR), Tailwind CSS 3.4.x (utility-first styling), Recharts 3.2.x (line, bar, pie, area, radar), Lucide React (icons). Module-based (type: module); ESLint, PostCSS, Autoprefixer. No React Router—section-based navigation via sidebar (Dashboard, Users, Call History, etc.).\n• Backend and services: Firebase (project goodmind-dca62) for Auth, Firestore, optional Hosting. Firebase Authentication (email/password; admin check via Firestore user.is_admin). Firestore as single source of truth (users, call_logs, conversations, assessments, notifications, mood_tracker, journal, onesignal_notifications, etc.). Groq API for AI-generated push notification content (e.g. openai/gpt-oss-120b). OneSignal for push delivery; dashboard sends via Cloud Function. Firebase Cloud Functions for backend logic (e.g. OneSignal API calls).\n• Deployment: Vercel (vercel.json) and Firebase Hosting (firebase.json). Service worker (sw.js), manifest, and PWA install prompt (InstallPWA component).\n\nFeatures: admin-only access\n\nAfter email/password login, the app checks Firestore user/{uid} for is_admin === true. Non-admins see an Access Denied screen.\n\n• Management Dashboard (Home): Stat cards (total users, active users last 30 days, total assessments, total calls). Charts: platform activity (area/bar), data distribution by collection (pie), weekly comparison, monthly growth (line). Database collections overview with live Firestore counts (user, call_logs, assessments, conversations, mood_tracker, journal, ff_push_notifications, onesignal_notifications, etc.). Responsive layout with loading and error states.\n• Users: User list from Firestore user collection (search, filters, sort). Filters: plan (Free Trial, Basic, Pro, Premium), date range (today, week, month, all). Sort: newest, oldest, name A–Z / Z–A. Stats: total users, admins, per-plan counts, active users, new users this month. Charts: plan distribution (pie), growth (bar). User detail modal: full profile (email, display name, plan, remaining time, conversation seconds, etc.).\n• Tara Calling and Call History: Tara Calling section links to or summarizes the Tara Calling PWA. Call History from Firestore call_logs: list and analytics. Stats: total calls, unique users, total/average duration, calls today/this week, longest call. Charts: daily calls and duration, duration distribution (e.g. 0–1 min, 1–5 min, 5+ min). Filters: search, date range.\n• Assessments: Data from Firestore assessments collection. Stats and tables for completion counts and trends; filtering and exploration.\n• Send Notification (with AI): Compose title (e.g. max 100 chars) and message (e.g. max 500 chars) with live preview and character counters. Send calls a Cloud Function that uses OneSignal API; on success, record written to Firestore onesignal_notifications. Generate by AI: modal where admin enters a short description (e.g. Remind users about daily meditation); app calls Groq with a mental-health-focused system prompt and returns suggested title and message in JSON; admin can edit and send. Stats: total notifications sent, sent today.\n• Notifications: View sent notifications (onesignal_notifications and related data); history and status of push campaigns.\n• Analytics: Platform analytics (totals for users, assessments, calls, notifications; average engagement per user). Charts: platform growth over time, collection distribution (pie), engagement metrics (completion rates, retention). Same Firestore collections as main dashboard.\n• Settings: App/config preferences; dashboard-specific or admin preferences.\n• UI/UX: Sidebar (desktop and mobile slide-out overlay), scroll-to-top button, user profile in sidebar, optional PWA install prompt. Theming via CSS variables (primary, accent, success, warning, card, sidebar) for a cohesive, modern look.\n\nHow the ecosystem fits together\n\nTara Calling (PWA): Users sign in, have voice/text conversations with TARA, complete assessments, log mood, use journal, receive push notifications; data flows to Firestore and call_logs. Firestore: Single source of truth for user, call_logs, conversations, assessments, mood_tracker, journal, ff_push_notifications, onesignal_notifications, tara, chatbot, etc. Mindspace.ai Dashboard: Reads (and where needed writes) the same Firestore collections; admins see users, calls, assessments, engagement; send push notifications; use Groq to draft notification copy. Cloud Functions: Server-side work (e.g. OneSignal API so keys stay off the client). So: Tara Calling produces data to Firestore; Mindspace.ai Dashboard consumes and partially writes it; Cloud Functions bridge dashboard, OneSignal, and other backend tasks.\n\nSecurity and configuration\n\nAuth: Firebase Auth (email/password); admin flag in Firestore user document. Firestore rules: users read/write own data; admins read (and where needed write) across collections. Secrets: Firebase config, Groq API key, OneSignal keys, Cloud Function URL in environment variables (e.g. VITE_* for Vite); sensitive keys in Cloud Functions where possible; documented in ENV_VARIABLES.md.\n\nWhy this stack works\n\nReact + TypeScript + Vite: fast iteration, clear types, small maintainable bundle. Tailwind: consistent, responsive UI with theming via CSS variables. Firebase: real-time data, auth, scalable backend with minimal custom server code. Recharts: product/engagement charts without a heavy BI tool. Groq: low-latency AI for empathetic, on-brand notification copy. OneSignal: reliable push delivery to Tara Calling. PWA + service worker: optional installable dashboard and offline caching for admins.",
    technologies: ["React 18", "TypeScript", "Vite 5", "Tailwind CSS", "Recharts", "Lucide React", "Firebase Auth", "Firestore", "Groq API", "OneSignal", "Firebase Cloud Functions", "Vercel", "PWA"],
