    title: "Aqsa Calligraphy: Luxury Islamic Calligraphy Website — Tech Stack, Features & SEO",
    brand: "Portfolio / E-commerce",
    metaDescription:
      "Aqsa Calligraphy (AAQSAA): luxury Islamic calligraphy portfolio and commission site. React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, Framer Motion. Gallery, services, commission form, Gmail SMTP, SEO, JSON-LD. Hyderabad artist Aqsa Rauf.",
    shortDescription:
      "Aqsa Calligraphy (AAQSAA) is a production-ready luxury calligraphy artist portfolio and commission platform for Aqsa Rauf (Hyderabad). React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, Framer Motion—gallery, services, commission form, contact via Gmail SMTP. SEO (meta, JSON-LD, sitemap), accessibility, dark theme and gold accents. Where every stroke tells a story.",
    imageUrl: "/images/portfolio/aqsa.png",
    tags: ["Portfolio", "Calligraphy", "Islamic Art", "React", "TypeScript", "Vite", "Tailwind", "Framer Motion", "SEO", "Vercel", "Commission"],
    longDescription:
      "Aqsa Calligraphy (Calligraphy by Aqsa / AAQSAA Calligraphy) is a production-ready luxury calligraphy artist portfolio and commission platform—a single-page application (SPA) that serves as the online home for Aqsa Rauf, a Hyderabad-based artist who creates handcrafted Islamic calligraphy art. The site showcases: portfolio and gallery (texture art, Quranic wall art, wedding calligraphy, custom name calligraphy, Blessed Beginnings collections); services (workshops, interior and spatial art B2B, products and merchandise, live wedding calligraphy, corporate gifting); commission workflow for custom orders (verses, names, wedding invitations, personalized artwork); and contact via a form that sends email (Gmail SMTP in production via Vercel serverless). The app is mobile-first, responsive, dark theme with gold accents, no database—contact submissions are email-only.\n\nFull tech stack\n\n• Frontend: React 18 (UI), TypeScript (type safety), Vite 5 (build, dev server, optimized bundles), Tailwind CSS 3 (utility-first, design tokens), Framer Motion (scroll and UI animations), Lucide React (icons), OGL (lightweight WebGL, hero/3D-style effects), React Router DOM 6 (client routing), React Helmet Async (per-route meta and SEO). Tooling: ESLint, PostCSS, Autoprefixer; path alias @/ to src.\n• Backend: Local dev—Flask 3 (Python) in server/contact_email.py on port 5000; Vite proxies /api to it. Production—Vercel serverless api/contact.py handles POST /api/contact, sends email via Gmail SMTP using env vars.\n• Config and deployment: Vercel (vercel.json: build, output dist, SPA fallback, Python serverless handlers). Env vars: EMAIL_SENDER, EMAIL_PASSWORD (Gmail App Password), EMAIL_RECEIVER (see server/.env.example). No database.\n\nAll application features\n\n• Pages and routes: / (Home: hero, about, masterpieces, services, CTA, FAQ, testimonials); /gallery (featured calligraphy); /services (workshops, interior and spatial art B2B, products and merchandise, live wedding calligraphy, corporate gifting); /commission (commission request form and info); /about (artist story—Aqsa Rauf, medico by profession artist by heart); /contact (form posts to /api/contact).\n• UI and behavior: Header (sticky nav, glassmorphism, mobile hamburger, smooth scroll, ARIA and keyboard); Hero (full-viewport, optional video background, gold/dark overlay); About (two-column, biography, arched image); Masterpieces (responsive grid, lazy-loaded images, hover, badges e.g. BEST SELLER, CUSTOM WORK); Services (cards with icons and hover); CTA, FAQ (accordion), Testimonials, Footer; ErrorBoundary; SEO (per-route meta title, description, keywords, canonical, OG image, JSON-LD Organization and WebSite); ScrollToTop on route change; LightRays (decorative gold overlay); primitives (SocialIcons WhatsApp/Instagram/YouTube, GlowingCards, ScrollTimeline, ThreeDScrollTrigger). Image right-click disabled; reduced-motion and high-contrast support.\n• Contact form and API: Frontend POST /api/contact (name, email, message). Dev: Flask sends via Gmail SMTP (server/.env). Prod: Vercel serverless same with Vercel env vars. No persistence.\n• SEO: Per-route meta; JSON-LD for LocalBusiness (Organization) and WebSite (SearchAction)—name, logo, image, founder, contact, address Hyderabad, social links, opening hours; public/sitemap.xml; semantic HTML and heading hierarchy.\n• Accessibility and performance: ARIA, keyboard nav, focus states (e.g. gold outline), semantic structure; font display swap; Vite code splitting (react-vendor, icons, ogl); lazy loading; ErrorBoundary.\n• Design system: Gold primary #d4af37, gold light #f9d976, dark primary #0a0f1a, dark secondary #0f1419, Persian teal; Playfair Display (headings), Inter (body), Cinzel (accents), Cormorant; gold gradient and outline buttons, glassmorphism header, card borders and hover; COLOR_PALETTE.md and design docs.\n\nCustom hooks: useMobileMenu (mobile menu state and keyboard), useScrollAnimation (Intersection Observer scroll animations).\n\nDeployment: npm run build (output dist), npm run preview (e.g. localhost:4173); Vercel—set EMAIL_SENDER, EMAIL_PASSWORD, EMAIL_RECEIVER, deploy; contact form uses /api/contact serverless. Optional: dist works for other static hosts; contact form needs backend or serverless if not Vercel.\n\nIn summary: Aqsa Calligraphy is a modern, production-ready portfolio and commission site built with React, TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind, plus a small Flask/Vercel backend for the contact form. Full feature set—gallery, services, commission flow, about, contact—with SEO (meta, canonical, JSON-LD, sitemap), accessibility (ARIA, keyboard, semantic HTML), and performance (code splitting, lazy loading, error boundaries). Tech stack and design system documented in README, PROJECT_SUMMARY, COLOR_PALETTE, DEPLOY. Deploy on Vercel with Gmail SMTP for contact emails.",
